{"id":"JMAP-510h.18","title":"Boilerplate explosion: 5 copies of identical Err(set_err)/Err(Other)/Err(_) match arms","description":"src/filenode.rs has 5 occurrences of the same 18-line match block translating BackendSetError into a JSON value (lines 273-294, 456-473, 547-564, 637-660, 685-702). The Err(_) catch-all is uniform; the Err(BackendSetError::SetError) → set_error_value() call is uniform; the Err(BackendSetError::Other) → serverFail JSON shape is uniform.

This is an obvious extract:

  fn backend_set_error_to_json<E: std::error::Error>(e: BackendSetError<E>) -> Value {
      match e {
          BackendSetError::SetError(set_err) => set_error_value(&set_err),
          BackendSetError::Other(e) => json!({ "type": "serverFail", "description": e.to_string() }),
          _ => json!({ "type": "serverFail", "description": "unhandled backend error variant" }),
      }
  }

Then each call site becomes:

  Err(e) => { not_created.insert(create_id, backend_set_error_to_json(e)); }

Reduces ~70 lines to ~5 + one helper. Also localizes the JMAP-510h.15 finding about the unactionable catch-all message into one place.

